    "problemStatement": "You have XXX 010101 strings and YYY 101010 strings. You will form a new string SSS by first rearranging these strings in some order, and then concatenate them in this **rearranged order**.\n\nLet f(S)f(S)f(S) denote the number of indices iii such that 1≤i&lt;∣S∣1 \\le i &lt; |S|1≤i&lt;∣S∣ and Si≠Si+1S_i \\ne S_{i + 1}Si​=Si+1​. Find the **minimum possible** value of f(S)f(S)f(S).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of input contains 222 integers - XXX and YYY.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum possible value of f(S)f(S)f(S).",
